2. RBAC / Custom Role Permissions
To adhere strictly to the Principle of Least Privilege, the Automation Account must not be granted generic Contributor roles. It requires a specific Custom Role containing only the exact actions needed to stop/start VMs and modify disk SKUs.

Required Actions for the Custom Role (e.g., Custom-Role-FinOps-ASR-SmartTiering):

Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines/read

Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines/powerOff/action

Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines/start/action

Microsoft.Compute/disks/read

Microsoft.Compute/disks/write

Microsoft.Compute/disks/revokeAccess/action

3. Assigning the Role at the Subscription Level
To ensure the automation scales effortlessly across all current and future DR Resource Groups, the role assignment is applied at the Subscription scope.

Navigate to the Subscription containing your ASR and DR resources.

[Screen: The Subscription overview page]

In the left-hand menu, select Access control (IAM).

Click + Add > Add role assignment.

[Screen: Dropdown menu showing "Add role assignment"]

In the Role tab, search for and select your newly created Custom Role (e.g., Custom-Role-FinOps-ASR-SmartTiering). Click Next.

